<section class="page-head">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="smallcaps section-no">Metals · The Second Desk</p>
    <h1>Ferrous and non-ferrous, traded with the same discipline.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Scrap and secondary metals move through the same house, on the same word. Smaller desk; same standards.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-no smallcaps">I. — Materials Handled</p>
    <div class="grade-table" role="table">
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Steel</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">HMS 1&amp;2, shredded, plate and structural. Prepared to ISRI basis, loaded in containers or bulk, weighbridge tickets supplied.</div></div>
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Aluminium</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">Extrusions, castings, used beverage cans, wheels. Clean, segregated, assay on request.</div></div>
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Cast iron</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">Machine breaks, engine blocks, demolition arisings. Drained, free of contamination.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-tinted">
  <div class="section-inner narrow">
    <p class="section-no smallcaps">II. — How the Desk Works</p>
    <p>Yards and works sell to us on regular programmes or single liftings. Export buyers take containerised and bulk material against the usual instruments. Descriptions are honest, weights are settled on the bridge, and claims — rare — are dealt with on evidence.</p>
    <p>The metals desk observes the Scrap Metal Dealers Act 2013 and the waste-carrier regime; licence particulars appear under <a class="quiet-link" href="/the-house">Compliance &amp; Accreditations</a> as they are granted.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/live-desk">Metal lots on the board</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

